Classify and preserve capture information on union types

Two union-type gaps in capture checking under strict mutability, which
together made types like `Unset | Array[Byte]` (Soundness's Optional[Data])
unusable:

- A union's inherited classifier fell through to its class symbols' common
  superclasses (Object, Matchable), whose classifier is Any, so a fresh
  capability instantiated for the union could never be re-absorbed at a local
  binding the way a bare Array's Unscoped-classified fresh is. The classifier
  is now the least upper bound of the members' classifiers, with always-pure
  members contributing nothing.

- CapturingType.apply dropped an empty capture set on a union unless every
  member derived from a capability trait, so the capability members
  re-acquired implied capture sets per occurrence, and two mentions of the
  same aliased union never matched. The empty set is now kept if any dealiased
  member derives from a capability trait.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude); source-level fixes for the affected
Soundness module were exhaustively ruled out before patching the compiler.

Enabled by `-Z:union-captures`; without it, upstream's code runs at every site this
patch touches.

